# Task 4 – Classes, Objects and Constructors

## Objective
To design Java classes and create objects using constructors.

## Classes and Fields
The ParkingTicket class stores the ticket number, vehicle number,
floor number and slot number.

## Constructors
1. Default Constructor: Creates a ticket with default values.
2. Parameterized Constructor: Creates a ticket using given values.
3. Copy Constructor: Creates a new ticket using the details of
   an existing ticket.

## this Keyword
The this keyword refers to the current object.
Constructor chaining is used to avoid repeated code.

## Memory Management
Reference variables refer to objects stored in heap memory.
Local reference variables are generally stored in stack frames.
Objects become eligible for garbage collection when they are
no longer reachable.

## Alternative Concept
Instead of overloaded constructors, objects can be created using
a default constructor followed by setter methods. However, this
may allow invalid objects to exist temporarily.

Static factory methods are another option for controlled object creation.

## Complexity Analysis
Creating n tickets takes O(n) total time.
The objects require O(n) total space.
Each ticket requires O(1) space for a fixed number of fields.

## Conclusion
Constructors help initialize objects properly and constructor
chaining reduces code duplication.